 Orders\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__child-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__child-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/nominations-appointments/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Nominations &amp; Appointments\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tNominations &amp; Appointments\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__child-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__child-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/presidential-memoranda/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Presidential Memoranda\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tPresidential Memoranda\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__child-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__child-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/proclamations/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Proclamations\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tProclamations\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</ul>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/fact-sheets/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Fact Sheets\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tFact Sheets\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link is-current\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Releases\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tReleases\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/remarks/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Remarks\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tRemarks\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/research/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Research\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tResearch\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</ul>\n\t\t</div>\n\t</nav>\n\t</div>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<p>Democrat New Jersey Gov. Mikie Sherrill <a href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/21/nyregion/noncitizen-voting-new-jersey-error.html\">admitted</a> today that a “software glitch” registered approximately 6,600 noncitizens to vote in her state between 2023 and 2024 — and hundreds of them actually cast ballots.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><a href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/21/nyregion/noncitizen-voting-new-jersey-error.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\" noreferrer noopener\"><img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"557\" height=\"333\" src=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/nyt-new-jersey-opt.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-45451\" style=\"width:400px\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>This is the direct result of Democrat policies that refuse basic citizenship checks — and exactly why Congress must pass the </strong><a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/saveamerica/\"><strong>SAVE America Act</strong></a> <strong>immediately. </strong>The bill <a href=\"https://www.congress.gov/crs-product/IF12902#:~:text=The%20bill%20would%20require%20states%2C%20within%2030%20days%20of%20enactment%2C%20to%20submit%20voter%20lists%20to%20the%20USCIS/DHS%20SAVE%20system%20to%20verify%20citizenship%20for%20voter%20eligibility.%20As%20indicated%20previously%2C%20states%20currently%20may%20use%20the%20system%20to%20verify%20voter%20eligibility.\">requires</a> states to use the Department of Homeland Security’s <a href=\"https://www.uscis.gov/save/about-save/about-save\">SAVE system</a> to confirm citizenship before registering anyone to vote in federal elections, a safeguard New Jersey has <a href=\"https://www.uscis.gov/save/about-save/save-agency-search-tool?%252Fviews%252Fajax%253F%252Fviews%252Fajax%253F%252Fviews%252Fajax%253F%252Fviews%252Fajax%253F%252Fviews%252Fajax%253Fbenefit_category%5B0%5D=97&amp;items_per_%252Fviews%252Fajax%253Fbenefit_category%5B0%5D=97&amp;%252Fviews%252Fajax%253F%252Fviews%252Fajax%253Fbenefit_category%5B0%5D=97&amp;%252Fviews%252Fajax%253F%252Fviews%252Fajax%253F%252Fviews%252Fajax%253Fbenefit_category%5B0%5D=97&amp;%252Fviews%252Fajax%253Fbenefit_category%5B0%5D=97&amp;topic_id=&amp;agency_state_code%5B0%5D=34&amp;agency_zip_code=&amp;benefit_category%5B0%5D=97&amp;benefit_category%5B1%5D=98&amp;markerVal=&amp;items_per_page=10\">refused to implement</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>The legislation also mandates voter ID for federal elections, a reform supported by the <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/2026/03/the-save-america-act-is-the-most-popular-election-reform-in-decades/\">overwhelming majority</a> of Americans, among other <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/2026/03/another-new-poll-shows-massive-support-for-save-america-act/\">popular initiatives</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Every illegal ballot dilutes the voice of a lawful American citizen and undermines election integrity.These incidents are not random errors; they are the predictable result of Democrat policies that refuse to verify citizenship.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>The American people demand secure elections. Congress must pass the SAVE America Act without delay.</strong></p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/2026/07/democrat-glitch-registers-thousands-of-noncitizens-to-vote-another-reason-to-pass-the-save-america-act/\">Democrat “Glitch” Registers Thousands of Noncitizens to Vote: Another Reason to Pass the SAVE America Act</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov\">The White House</a>.</p>",
